---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Frequently Asked Questions | Fictional History Archive">
  <div class="border-b-2 border-archive-border pb-4 mb-8">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-archive-paper mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-archive-muted">
      System Queries & Protocol Clarifications
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <section class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-6">
      <h2 class="font-sans text-lg font-bold text-archive-accent mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">What is the Fictional History Archive?</h2>
      <p class="font-serif text-archive-paper leading-relaxed">
        The Archive is an independent, multiversal repository designed to chronicle and preserve the most significant historical events across various alternate realities, cinematic universes, literary dimensions, and speculative timelines. We catalog the impossible so it remains unforgotten.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-6">
      <h2 class="font-sans text-lg font-bold text-archive-accent mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">Are these events real?</h2>
      <p class="font-serif text-archive-paper leading-relaxed">
        Within their own localized timelines, absolutely. From a prime-Earth perspective, these events are drawn from works of fiction (literature, film, television, interactive media). The Archive presents them strictly as factual historical records within the context of their native universes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-6">
      <h2 class="font-sans text-lg font-bold text-archive-accent mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">How do I submit a historical record?</h2>
      <p class="font-serif text-archive-paper leading-relaxed">
        Archivists in the field may submit new entries using the Contribute terminal. Submissions must adhere strictly to the guidelines outlined in the Archivist's Handbook, maintaining a journalistic tone and focusing on events of massive cultural or timeline-shifting significance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-6">
      <h2 class="font-sans text-lg font-bold text-archive-accent mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">Why are there multiple accounts of the same date?</h2>
      <p class="font-serif text-archive-paper leading-relaxed">
        Temporal anomalies frequently result in intersecting timelines. When different realities document conflicting events on the exact same Earth date, our Multiversal Perspective protocol activates, allowing you to cross-reference the divergent historical records side-by-side.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
